===Draw===
{{Main|2018 FIFA World Cup seeding}}

[[File:Fabio Cannavaro 2017.jpg|thumb|upright|[[Italians|Italian]] World Cup winner [[Fabio Cannavaro]] in [[Moscow]] at the 2018 World Cup draw]]
The draw was held on 1 December 2017 at 18:00 [[Moscow Time|MSK]] at the [[State Kremlin Palace]] in Moscow.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2017/m=1/news=final-draw-to-take-place-in-state-kremlin-palace-2864946.html |title=Final Draw to take place in State Kremlin Palace |date=24 January 2017 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171116185925/https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/y=2017/m=1/news=final-draw-to-take-place-in-state-kremlin-palace-2864946.html |archive-date=16 November 2017}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/0/world-cup-draw-2018-date-time-does-start-could-england-get/ |title=Final Draw to take place at 18:00 |date=24 November 2017 |website=The Daily Telegraph |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171125212925/http://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/0/world-cup-draw-2018-date-time-does-start-could-england-get/ |archive-date=25 November 2017}}</ref> The draw was conducted by former footballer [[Gary Lineker]] alongside Russian sports journalist {{ill|Maria Komandnaya|ru|Командная, Мария Дмитриевна}}, with several well-known football personalities assisting, including [[Diego Maradona]], [[Fabio Cannavaro]], [[Cafu]], [[Diego Forlán]], [[Gordon Banks]], [[Carles Puyol]], [[Laurent Blanc]], and former Russian player [[Nikita Simonyan]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/the-final-draw-in-numbers-2921836 |title=The Final Draw in numbers |publisher=FIFA |date=29 November 2017 |access-date=26 June 2026 |archive-date=20 April 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240420072343/https://inside.fifa.com/tournaments/mens/worldcup/2018russia/news/the-final-draw-in-numbers-2921836 |url-status=live }}</ref><ref>{{cite web |last=McMahon |first=Bobby |url=https://www.forbes.com/sites/bobbymcmahon/2017/11/30/everything-you-need-to-know-about-the-2018-world-cup-final-draw-and-some-stuff-you-dont/ |title=Everything You Need To Know About The 2018 World Cup Final Draw And Some Stuff You Probably Don't |publisher=Forbes |date=30 November 2017 |access-date=26 June 2026 |archive-date=6 May 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260506052605/https://www.forbes.com/sites/bobbymcmahon/2017/11/30/everything-you-need-to-know-about-the-2018-world-cup-final-draw-and-some-stuff-you-dont/ |url-status=live }}</ref> The 32 teams were drawn into eight groups of four, by selecting one team from each of the four ranked pots.

For the draw, the teams were allocated to four pots based entirely on the [[FIFA World Rankings]] of October 2017. Pot one contained the hosts Russia (who were automatically assigned to position A1) and the best seven teams. Pot two contained the next best eight teams, and so on for pots three and four.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/news/y=2017/m=9/news=oc-for-fifa-competitions-approves-procedures-for-the-final-draw-of-the-2907924.html |title=OC for FIFA Competitions approves procedures for the Final Draw of the 2018 FIFA World Cup |date=14 September 2017 |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20171110171903/https://www.fifa.com/about-fifa/news/y=2017/m=9/news=oc-for-fifa-competitions-approves-procedures-for-the-final-draw-of-the-2907924.html |archive-date=10 November 2017}}</ref> This was different from previous draws, when only pot one was based on FIFA rankings while the remaining pots were based on geographical considerations. However, teams from the same confederation still were not drawn against each other for the group stage, except that two UEFA teams could be in each group. The pots for the draw are shown below.<ref>{{Cite web |title=2018 FIFA World Cup - News - The Final Draw: How it works |website=FIFA.com |publisher=Fédération Internationale de Football Association |access-date=6 April 2020 |url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/the-final-draw-how-it-works-2921565 |archive-date=6 April 2020 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20200406194931/https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/news/the-final-draw-how-it-works-2921565 |url-status=live}}</ref>

