===Discipline===
In total, only four players were sent off in the entire tournament, the fewest since [[1978 FIFA World Cup|1978]].<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.espn.co.uk/football/fifa-world-cup/4/blog/post/3567494/fifa-world-cup-by-the-numbers-most-goals-in-the-knockoutspogba-first-ever-united-player-to-score-in-final |title=World Cup by the numbers - 169 goals, 29 penalties, 10 late winners, 4 red cards |publisher=ESPN |date=16 July 2018 |access-date=17 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180717165744/http://www.espn.co.uk/football/fifa-world-cup/4/blog/post/3567494/fifa-world-cup-by-the-numbers-most-goals-in-the-knockoutspogba-first-ever-united-player-to-score-in-final |archive-date=17 July 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref> [[International Football Association Board]] technical director [[David Elleray]] stated a belief that this was due to the introduction of [[Video assistant referee|VAR]], since players would know that they would not be able to get away with anything under the new system.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/06/17/var-credited-cleaning-world-cup-no-red-cards-nine-games/ |title=VAR effect results in cleanest World Cup since 1986 after no red cards are issued in opening 11 games |work=The Telegraph |date=17 June 2018 |access-date=17 July 2018 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180618084905/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/world-cup/2018/06/17/var-credited-cleaning-world-cup-no-red-cards-nine-games/ |archive-date=18 June 2018 |url-status=live}}</ref>

A player is automatically suspended for the next match for the following offences:<ref name="regulations">{{cite web |url=https://digitalhub.fifa.com/m/74fabee6a36ad3b2/original/ejmfg94ac7hypl9zmsys-pdf.pdf |title=Regulations – 2018 FIFA World Cup Russia |publisher=FIFA |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20170712134322/http://resources.fifa.com/mm/document/tournament/competition/02/84/35/19/regulationsfwc2018en_neutral.pdf |archive-date=12 July 2017}}</ref>
* Receiving a red card (red card suspensions may be extended for serious offences)
* Receiving two yellow cards in two matches; yellow cards expire after the completion of the quarter-finals (yellow card suspensions are not carried forward to any other future international matches)

